    <rdfs:label>PROBE B1 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a nodule that is both solid and part-solid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Value disjointness. Without it, a single-select element is single-select only by convention. Note this bites through someValuesFrom because the value classes are disjoint, not because of any cardinality axiom. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="n4404ee68d158488e83d8f931eae8c061b25"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. Value disjointness. Without it, a single-select element is single-select only by convention. Note this bites through someValuesFrom because the value classes are disjoint, not because of any cardinality axiom.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000043_Isoechoic">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>isoechoic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/EchogenicityValue"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000044_Hyperechoic"/>
    <skos:definition>Equal in echogenicity to the adjacent parenchyma.</skos:definition>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://radlex.org/RID/RID6047"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>isoechoic</skos:prefLabel>
    <cde:conceptSource>BI-RADS 5, BI-RADS 4, TI-RADS, LI-RADS 2020</cde:conceptSource>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:created>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-V_000043_Isoechoic-RADLEX-RID6047"/>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:lastModified>
    <cde:localId>V-000043</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>Value</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:rank rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</cde:rank>
    <cde:sourceDefinition>BI-RADS US: having the same echogenicity as subcutaneous fat. [TI-RADS]: Similar echogenicity relative to thyroid tissue [LI-RADS] Echogenicity equal to background liver</cde:sourceDefinition>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>proposed</cde:versionStatus>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000164_FluidFluidLevel">
