    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n18ec46086f304a00955c944e6c60b2e7b663"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/FindingClass"/>
    <skos:definition>Blood within the cranial cavity. The compartment it occupies is the clinically decisive fact and is carried by the subtypes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>intracranial hemorrhage</skos:prefLabel>
    <cde:anchorBase rdf:resource="http://radlex.org/RID/RID4700"/>
    <cde:anchorModifier rdf:resource="http://radlex.org/RID/RID6383"/>
    <cde:anchorVerdict>post_coordinated</cde:anchorVerdict>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:created>
    <cde:designNote>Anchored to the intracranial region, so it is a class rather than an abstraction. Acute versus chronic is a temporal-descriptor value on the class, not a further subtype: RadLex carries acute and chronic as children of temporal descriptor and has no acute-haemorrhage concept.</cde:designNote>
