  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A2_NoduleInSuperiorSegmentRLL">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A2 [EXPECT SUBCLASS of an existing class - yellow row in SubClass Of, moves in the tree when the dropdown is set to Inferred]: a nodule in the superior segment of the right lower lobe</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Three partOf steps: segment -&gt; lower lobe -&gt; right lung, then one subsumption step right lung -&gt; lung. The mixed chain named in classifier-placement-considerations.md. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="n4404ee68d158488e83d8f931eae8c061b5"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by PulmonaryNodule. Three partOf steps: segment -&gt; lower lobe -&gt; right lung, then one subsumption step right lung -&gt; lung. The mixed chain named in classifier-placement-considerations.md.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000224_NearOcclusion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>near-occlusion</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/NarrowingDegreeValue"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000223_Occluded"/>
    <skos:definition>The distal lumen is collapsed rather than merely narrowed, so a percentage understates it. Read from the string sign rather than from a ratio, which is why it is a band and never a number.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>near-occlusion</skos:prefLabel>
