    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="la">arteria cerebri anterior</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>Artery formed by the bifurcation of the internal carotid artery (carotid artery, internal). Branches of the anterior cerebral artery supply the caudate nucleus; internal CAPSULE; putamen; septal nuclei; gyrus cinguli; and surfaces of the frontal lobe and parietal lobe. [MeSH]</skos:definition>
