  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/anatomy/RID28538">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>airspace</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/AnatomicLocation"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/anatomy/RID1296"/>
    <skos:definition>Anatomy.—An airspace is the gas-containing part of the lung, including the respiratory bronchioles but excluding purely conducting airways, such as terminal bronchioles. 
Radiographs and CT scans.—This term is used in conjunction with consolidation, opacity, and nodules to designate the filling of airspaces with the products of disease (14).  [Fleischner Society]</skos:definition>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://radlex.org/RID/RID28538"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>airspace</skos:prefLabel>
    <cde:conceptSource>Fleischner Society</cde:conceptSource>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:created>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-RID28538-RADLEX-RID28538"/>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:lastModified>
    <cde:localId>AL-000149</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>AnatomicLocation</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:source>imported</cde:source>
    <cde:sourceDefinition>Anatomy.—An airspace is the gas-containing part of the lung, including the respiratory bronchioles but excluding purely conducting airways, such as terminal bronchioles. 
Radiographs and CT scans.—This term is used in conjunction with consolidation, opacity, and nodules to designate the filling of airspaces with the products of disease (14).  [Fleischner Society]</cde:sourceDefinition>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>published</cde:versionStatus>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/HeartFailure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>heart failure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n18ec46086f304a00955c944e6c60b2e7b308"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n18ec46086f304a00955c944e6c60b2e7b309"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n18ec46086f304a00955c944e6c60b2e7b310"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/Diagnosis"/>
    <skos:definition>Inability of the heart to maintain adequate output, with venous congestion.</skos:definition>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://radlex.org/RID/RID34795"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/84114007"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>heart failure</skos:prefLabel>
    <cde:anchorVerdict>anchored</cde:anchorVerdict>
    <cde:conceptSource>Playbook</cde:conceptSource>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:created>
    <cde:designNote>Causes the oedema rather than manifesting as it: heart failure raises left atrial pressure and fluid accumulates, which is production of a second entity. Nothing here shows itself as anything, which is why it has no manifestation edge at all. Carried as a node so causal edges have a target; it has no imaging elements of its own and is not something a radiologist reports seeing.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-HeartFailure-RADLEX-RID34795"/>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-HeartFailure-SNOMEDCT-84114007"/>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-10</cde:lastModified>
    <cde:localId>DX-000015</cde:localId>
    <cde:noImagingElements rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</cde:noImagingElements>
    <cde:nodeType>Diagnosis</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>proposed</cde:versionStatus>
  </rdf:Description>
