  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/C3_ProgressionWithinOneClass">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE C3 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: a cyst that may progress to a cyst</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The shape that actually works: progression within one class, where what changes is the value of an attribute rather than the class. RadLex models acute and chronic this way, as children of temporal descriptor RID5716, and carries no 'acute hemorrhage' or 'chronic hemorrhage' concept at all. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="n4404ee68d158488e83d8f931eae8c061b63"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group C] expect: SATISFIABLE. The shape that actually works: progression within one class, where what changes is the value of an attribute rather than the class. RadLex models acute and chronic this way, as children of temporal descriptor RID5716, and carries no 'acute hemorrhage' or 'chronic hemorrhage' concept at all.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
